intro_legal_text#:#<p><strong>Original development:</strong> André Schweigert and Cornel Musielak.<br>Institution: Friedrich-Alexander-Universität Erlangen-Nürnberg (FAU).</p><p>License: <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GNU AGPLv3 (AGPL-3.0-only)</a>, supplemented by the attribution preservation term under section 7(b) in the accompanying NOTICE file. The plugin is provided without warranty within the terms of the license. Redistribution and modification are permitted under the license terms.</p><p>Project and source code: <a href="https://github.com/andreschweigert/ExtendedTestSettings" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ExtendedTestSettings on GitHub</a>.</p>
intro_about_text#:#<p>The <strong>ExtendedTestSettings</strong> plugin extends ILIAS tests with additional features for online and on-site exams – such as calculators, special character palettes, exam protection, time warnings or connection monitoring. The features are bundled into independent <strong>modules</strong> that can be installed, activated, deactivated and updated independently of the plugin core.</p>
intro_usage_manage_title#:#Manage modules
intro_usage_manage_desc#:#On the "Modules" tab, modules are uploaded as a ZIP package, activated or deactivated and updated to new versions. Installed modules are stored in the modules/ directory.
intro_usage_pertest_title#:#Configure per test
intro_usage_pertest_desc#:#In every test, the "Extended Test Settings" sub-tab appears under Settings. There, each active module offers its own configuration fields – changes apply only to the respective test.
intro_support_text#:#<p>The documentation of the individual modules can be found on GitHub: <a href="%1$s" target="_blank" rel="noopener">%1$s</a></p><p>If you have any problems or questions, feel free to send an email to <a href="mailto:andre.schweigert@fau.de">andre.schweigert@fau.de</a> or create an issue on GitHub.</p><p>The development of new modules is also welcome – information on this will follow. <strong>Module requests</strong> can be submitted at any time as well.</p>
